&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our customers come from all walks of life and so do we. We hire great people from a wide variety of backgrounds, not just because it&#39;s the right thing to do, but because it makes our company stronger. If you share our values and our enthusiasm for small businesses, you will find a home at Gusto.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Gusto is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate in hiring or any employment decision based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. Gusto considers qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Gusto is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. We want to see our candidates perform to the best of their ability. If you require a medical or religious accommodation at any time throughout your candidate journey, please fill out &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdEfl7Bp-Twz7LLlhGlha46CrxZ9Kacgakmarf3K2TbnaEgKQ/viewform&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt; and a member of our team will get in touch with you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gusto takes security and protection of your personal information very seriously. Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/fraudulent-activity-disclaimer&quot;&gt;Fraudulent Activity Disclaimer&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Personal information collected and processed as part of your Gusto application will be subject to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/about/careers/applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Gusto&#39;s Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;374&quot; data-end=&quot;399&quot;&gt;About the team + role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;401&quot; data-end=&quot;843&quot;&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;845&quot; data-end=&quot;1229&quot;&gt;The Android team’s mission is to redefine how millions of users engage with their finances. We&#39;re focused on delivering intuitive, scalable, and inclusive mobile experiences that empower our customers to build better financial futures. We collaborate closely with Product, Design, and Backend Engineering to ensure every interaction on Android reflects quality, performance, and care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Trading Products team&lt;/strong&gt; creates the experiences that bring Robinhood’s trading ecosystem to life for customers every day. Team Experience is responsible for making those journeys feel fast, intuitive, and dependable—so customers can engage with sophisticated trading products through simple, well-crafted mobile experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1491&quot; data-end=&quot;1596&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1598&quot; data-end=&quot;1824&quot;&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;1831&quot; data-end=&quot;1849&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the technical direction for Android experiences across high-impact product areas, building intuitive, elegant, and reliable mobile systems using Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and modern Android APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex, ambiguous initiatives end to end—from early product and technical strategy through architecture, implementation, experimentation, launch, and long-term evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Managers, Designers, Backend Engineers, and Data Scientists to shape roadmaps, influence product decisions, and deliver solutions that create meaningful customer and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and uphold engineering standards, architecture patterns, and development practices thatimprove quality, scalability, maintainability, and developer velocity across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a technical leader and multiplier by mentoring engineers, driving design reviews, unblocking critical decisions, and raising the overall bar for execution, craftsmanship, and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;2396&quot; data-end=&quot;2399&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2401&quot; data-end=&quot;2419&quot;&gt;What you bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2422&quot; data-end=&quot;2491&quot;&gt;8+ years of professional experience developing Android applications, including experience leading large-scale or technically complex mobile initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2422&quot; data-end=&quot;2491&quot;&gt;Deep proficiency with Kotlin and/or Java, and strong expertise in Android SDK fundamentals and architecture patterns such as MVVM, with a track record of making sound architectural tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2422&quot; data-end=&quot;2491&quot;&gt;Strong experience with Jetpack Compose, Coroutines and Flow or RxJava, and common Android libraries such as Retrofit and Room, with the ability to apply them at scale in complex production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2422&quot; data-end=&quot;2491&quot;&gt;Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to influence cross-functional partners and align teams around technical and product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2422&quot; data-end=&quot;2491&quot;&gt;Demonstrated track record of leading through ambiguity, driving architecture across multiple projects or surfaces, and mentoring senior engineers while elevating engineering standards beyond your immediate team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2422&quot; data-end=&quot;2491&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;2961&quot; data-end=&quot;2964&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2966&quot; data-end=&quot;2983&quot;&gt;What we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2986&quot; data-end=&quot;3037&quot;&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3040&quot; data-end=&quot;3165&quot;&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3168&quot; data-end=&quot;3276&quot;&gt;Best-in-class benefits including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3279&quot; data-end=&quot;3376&quot;&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3379&quot; data-end=&quot;3469&quot;&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3472&quot; data-end=&quot;3554&quot;&gt;Generous time off including company holidays, PTO, sick time, and parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3557&quot; data-end=&quot;3648&quot;&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, stocked kitchens, and commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1598&quot; data-end=&quot;1824&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$270,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$203,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$238,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$211,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Usage Disclosure:&lt;/strong&gt; Robinhood uses artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of our recruiting process. These tools enhance the efficiency and consistency of our hiring process; however, all hiring decisions are made by our hiring teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a Director, Corporate Development to join our team in Culver City, USA,&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;on a hybrid basis. We can support with visa sponsorship and relocation assistance from any location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day – whether in our work environments alongside talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing, and innovating in the mobile games industry, connecting millions of players around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Development team identifies, evaluates &amp;amp; executes potential M&amp;amp;A, investment, and partnership opportunities. We utilize market and product data to inform decisions around our M&amp;amp;A strategy and execution, including building detailed analyses for review by our executive team when evaluating potential partnership opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Corporate Development, reporting to the VP of Corporate Development, you will help drive Scopely&#39;s investment and strategic partnership activity with game studios worldwide. You will originate, negotiate, and close deals directly with founders and C-level executives at target studios, as well as with the investment banks and advisors representing the other side of the transaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage relationships with studio founder/s, executives, investment banks, financial advisors, and other industry partners to develop a global deal pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead execution of investment and strategic partnership transactions with game studios globally, from sourcing through close and post-deal enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Scopely&#39;s Legal, Finance, and Tax teams to structure deals, including equity investments, incentive structure, tax treatment, and risk allocation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate directly with C-level executives at target studios and with investment banks and financial advisors representing the other side of the deal, on valuation, terms, and structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and lead weekly meetings with Scopely&#39;s C-suite to review deal negotiations and the broader deal pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, coach, and support the development of at least one direct report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Articulate Scopely&#39;s vision, capabilities, and operating model to studio founders, executives, and their advisors, and identify how Scopely can best partner with each studio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel internationally, with an understanding of how business and deal-making norms vary by region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor industry trends, emerging studios, new releases, and competitive activity through market research, gameplay industry events, and conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of corporate development, investment banking, private equity, venture capital, M&amp;amp;A, consulting, or business development experience, ideally with exposure to games or interactive entertainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated track record of personally negotiating and closing investment, partnership, or M&amp;amp;A transactions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of deal structuring, valuation, and the legal, financial, and tax considerations involved in structuring investments and strategic partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing, coaching, or mentoring team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the video game or interactive entertainment industry, or the ability to learn industry dynamics quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and comfort running recurring deal reviews with senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build trust with founders, executives, and advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, entrepreneurial approach; a self-starter focused on improving how Scopely partners with studios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking, sound judgment, and the ability to balance deal value, risk, and long-term partnership potential&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally and collaborate across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with game studios or other IP-led businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with gaming business models, market trends, and industry performance indicators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across different regions and cultural environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that!&amp;nbsp; We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$164,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$247,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain high-scale, distributed systems to work with the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within a team to build the core networking solutions, which include load balancing, mTLS networking, fleet health &amp;amp; observability used by product teams to build and operate microservices supporting the company’s business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a great customer experience for internal company teams using Infra and play a key role in enabling the company’s Infra to power all of the company’s products globally and at scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, design, implement, and deploy robust solutions, making appropriate tradeoffs between reliability, throughput, latency, resiliency, engineering, velocity, and cost.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate, design, and implement software solutions that contribute towards improvement and resiliency, reliability, efficiency, and management at scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to team strategy, roadmap, tooling, process, and culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear goals and provide regular feedback on team member performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s Degree or foreign equivalent degree in Computer Science, or a related field, plus five (5) years of post-bachelor&#39;s progressive work experience in software engineering. In the alternative, the employer is willing to accept a Master&#39;s Degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, or a related field, plus three (3) years of experience in Software Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have three (3) years of experience in the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software development including in Cloud systems, AWS, Azure, GCP, and OCI;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating technical architecture and design;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building an operating infrastructure and tools that empower developers;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing software using Java and GO;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing, maintaining and debugging distributed systems built with open source tools;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Breaking down large, complex systems, identifying shortcomings and optimization opportunities, and making data drive cost performance tradeoffs to influence design decisions; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizing systems and tools including: Kubernetes, EC2, Envoy, Linux, and Puppet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $221,187 – $285,600/yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;100% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends. CA50&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-DNI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and operating critical, large-scale systems that manage massive volumes of financial information, to fulfill business goals for Stripe and its partners;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate a complex fintech environment with numerous compliance regulations, translating internal and external business needs into robust software requirements and scalable distributed systems;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross- functional alignment and provide technical direction for multi-team projects;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build large-scale (petabyte-size) financial data platforms, solutions, and pipelines using Big Data technologies and distributed systems;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debugging production issues across the stack, analyzing complex datasets and designing large-scale data pipelines using modern Big Data technologies to ensure reliable, high-performance solutions;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executing projects related to insights into Stripe’s financial performance across multiple Stripe products;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on systems critical to Stripe&#39;s future financial operations, with impact over billions of dollars of payment volume;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the design and architecture of modern payments and financial technology across countries; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage experience with monitoring, incident handling, debugging in production environments to ensure data pipeline health and SLOs, while reducing operational toil via automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s Degree or foreign equivalent degree in Computer Science, Information Systems Security, or a related field, plus five (5) years of related work experience in Software Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience programming in Java, Scala, or Python;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience designing, building, and maintaining scalable distributed systems;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience debugging production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience with different testing tools and frameworks including JUnit, Mockito, and TestNG;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years of experience developing complex SQL queries, analyzing datasets and designing large-scale data pipelines;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years of experience working in fintech domain;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years of experience leading cross-team projects and building alignment on multi-team technical direction; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 year experience working with Apache Spark or similar modern Big Data technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $206,086.00 - $285,600.00/yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions / sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends. &lt;strong&gt;WA80&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
